      "writtenOn": "2017-05-12T03:30:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when waiting for bit intervals, you should not be waiting for fixed duration, you should be waiting for the next moment in time when bit interval expires. \n\nthis way you can accommodate the slack of variable execution time. (like going into ones++ or not in line 188), and even can calculate the next bit value while the current one is being transmitted.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 182,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 182,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "e75089918addf329effe84b2fcdc5263b6266dda",
