      "writtenOn": "2017-05-11T23:20:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Potentially want to wait a little over bit_period_us to ensure when the line is sampled it has had time to transition and settle. The interrupt latency gives you some. Maybe even 1.5*bit_period_us. Also will help in the case where the transmitter clock is running a little slow (so its effective bit_period_us is longer than you expect potentially meaning that by the time you get to the end of the byte you sample early).",
